# Project: CSV Data Analyst Web App

## Mandatory startup behavior
1. Read `AGENTS.md` at the project root first.
2. Read the relevant feature plan in `docs/features/` if the task matches a feature.
3. Summarize stack, architecture, and conventions before writing any code.
4. Do not start coding if requirements are ambiguous — ask concise questions first.

## Stack (quick reference)
- Next.js 15 App Router + TypeScript strict
- Tailwind CSS v4
- TanStack Table v8 + PapaParse
- Recharts + react-grid-layout
- Vercel AI SDK + Google Gemini 2.0 Flash
- Zustand for global state

## Hard rules
- All types live in `src/types/index.ts` — never duplicate.
- All AI calls go through `/api/chat` — never from client.
- All chart rendering goes through `ChartRenderer.tsx`.
- Zustand only for shared state — no localStorage for CSV row data.
- Server Components for shells, Client Components for interactive UI.
- Every component must handle loading, empty, and error states.
- Tailwind only — no inline styles except react-grid-layout dimensions.
- Minimal diffs. Reuse existing code before creating new abstractions.
- No broad refactors unless explicitly requested.

